        "messages": [
          {
            "content": "<@&1562228542274797608>\nAiO Command Menu -Reforger- — 0.4.1\nhttps://reforger.armaplatform.com/workshop/629405AEFC950C12\nPart 1/1 · relay 8ee78dcc6ec9cf1e:1\n\n0.4.1\r\n\r\nBug fixes for Fire on my lead, Stealth and squads you take over.\r\n\r\nFIXED\r\n\r\n- Fire on my lead: men walking a route or patrol keep holding fire past each waypoint; switching to a weapon with fewer rounds loaded or reloading no longer counts as your first shot; and a man given a new order mid-fight (Move here, Halt, Follow) goes back to his earlier fire rules afterwards instead of firing at will for good.\r\n- Stealth: leaving it no longer leaves return fire on for good, and a fire rule you gave while in Stealth is kept when you switch to Aware, Safe or Combat.\r\n- A squad you took over keeps its commander's objective through fire-rule, stance, engine, lights, Heal up, Rearm, ammo and bandage, Take weapon, seat change, Unflip and Suppress orders. It is replaced only once a man actually carries out your order, so a Take cover that finds no cover or a Garrison with no free post leaves it in place.\r\n- In a squad you took over, an order to selected men that covers every living man counts as a whole-squad order; an order to only some of them keeps the commander's objective.\r\n- Eject: a man the game won't let bail out keeps his orders, and the reply no longer claims nobody was in a vehicle.",
